{"pageProps":{"story":{"name":"INTERFACE OF HUMANITY","created_at":"2025-06-16T13:51:57.429Z","published_at":"2025-06-16T14:10:00.980Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T14:10:00.996Z","id":688259618,"uuid":"5816c66a-8b02-4538-a619-03d636222f78","content":{"_uid":"a9af7d85-4805-4329-b71b-f5b2dea94b84","title":"INTERFACE OF HUMANITY","video":[],"client":"NTT Human Informatics Laboratories","modules":[{"_uid":"0a74c20f-e75a-43ec-9d1b-2cecd8b55645","quote":"In a world where over 1.3 billion people live with disabilities, NTT’s innovative project reimagines what it means to participate in society. By developing adaptive user interfaces powered by electromyography (EMG), eye-gaze, haptic, and brainwave technologies, the project empowers bedridden individuals to express themselves, compete, and connect through gaming and music. This initiative not only bridges the gap between disabled and able-bodied individuals but also pioneers a future where physical limitations no longer equate to social exclusion.","credit":"","component":"quote_block","use_accent_color":true},{"_uid":"6dc9cf4c-a526-4611-9ce5-6323e39d0b33","image":{"id":23160522,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/3840x2160/2536831493/iot-2.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"full-width","use_accent_color":true,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"218fe07d-0ec5-481d-974c-9a15d53800ca","text":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":6},"content":[{"text":"Challenge ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"text":"Breaking the Barrier of Social Isolation for the Bedridden","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Millions of people with severe physical disabilities, including 2.3 million bedridden individuals in Japan alone, face extreme limitations in communication, education, and employment. Traditional interfaces and social platforms fail to accommodate their needs, leaving them isolated and unable to participate in everyday activities or express their creativity.","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]}]},"component":"rich_text","use_accent_color":false},{"_uid":"d22e6591-6d16-4e08-9565-f4782d8d6ca5","image":{"id":23160576,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2972x1672/4c0e0976bb/iot-3.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"small","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"7ef26c26-79c5-43a6-afa2-dff98c698d98","text":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":6},"content":[{"text":"Approach ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"text":"Harnessing Emerging Technologies for Inclusive Interaction","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"NTT Human Informatics Laboratories collaborated with individuals with disabilities to co-develop adaptive interfaces using EMG, eye-gaze, haptic, and brainwave inputs. These interfaces were connected to digital avatars and gaming platforms like Minecraft and VRChat, enabling intuitive control and immersive experiences. The team conducted extensive R&D, including sensor optimization and noise reduction, to ensure seamless and personalized interaction.","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]}]},"component":"rich_text","use_accent_color":false},{"_uid":"5904d2c4-c007-4187-84bb-9edc157c7b43","images":[{"id":23160605,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2154x1215/9d589877d8/iot-4.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{}},{"id":23160609,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/1744x1744/79137a6331/iot-5.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{}},{"id":23160612,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2157x1218/a132c37538/iot-6.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{}}],"component":"image_grid_fluid","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"ce93afed-f994-40f8-8606-5712fec90d0c","text":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":6},"content":[{"text":"Solution ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"text":"CREATING a New Form of Embodiment Through Play","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"The project introduced the world’s first interface allowing bedridden individuals to become active players in virtual environments. Participants used EMG signals from their neck, arms, or legs to control avatars, perform live music, and compete in eSports events. These experiences were made accessible globally through free applications, and showcased at major events like Cannes Lions, SXSW, and Ars Electronica, proving that physical limitations need not hinder creativity or connection.","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]}]},"component":"rich_text","use_accent_color":false},{"_uid":"f86402c6-758c-4eb9-9423-16dca8183d56","image":{"id":23160621,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2972x1672/d2233b1d07/iot-7.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"small","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"718c68d7-3835-454f-b307-672d09e5f8e0","values":[{"_uid":"64c95771-ce1a-42b9-9cc0-a5a7d29eaf2b","number":"4","component":"statistic","unit_left":"","uni